    "title": "Tennessee Titans injury report: Tyjae Spears returns, Blake Hance sits - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Serena Burks ,\n1 hours ago Sep 30, 2024; Miami Gardens, Florida, USA; Tennessee Titans running back Tyjae Spears (2) runs with the football against the Miami Dolphins during the second quarter at Hard Rock Stadium. Mandatory Credit: Sam Navarro-Imagn Images By Sam Navarro-Imagn Images The Tennessee Titans hit the field on Wednesday for their first round of practices ahead of their meeting with the Arizona Cardinals in Phoenix, Arizona, this Sunday at 3:05 p.m. CDT.\nThe Titans are winless through the first four weeks of play, losing by a larger margin each week. On paper, this team looks improved over last season, but that hasn't translated to the field. The Cardinals are 2-2, coming off two consecutive losses to the San Francisco 49ers and Seattle Seahawks .\nAside from the six players on injured reserve, the injuries to available players haven't been heavy. Tyjae Spears' 21-day return window opened when he practiced earlier today, but J.C. Latham is still nursing that hip injury.\nThe Titans' full injury report is below.\nDid not participate OL Blake Hance (shoulder) OL J.C. Latham (hip) WR Bryce Oliver (knee) WR Calvin Ridley (knee/elbow) Limited participation S Mike Brown (knee) DL James Lynch (shoulder) RB Tony Pollard (NIR - rest) DT Jeffery Simmons (NIR - rest) RB Tyjae Spears (knee) S Kevin Winston Jr. (hamstring) G Kevin Zeitler (foot) Full participation None This article originally appeared on Titans Wire: Tennessee Titans injury report: Tyjae Spears returns, Blake Hance sits",
